  "notes": [
    "Independently read all five eligible production source files and both metadata files; all 14 plugin-root files are partitioned. Every file matches the pinned commit byte-for-byte. No plugin-local AGENTS.md exists; root, extensions, plugins and plugin-sdk instructions were read.",
    "All production relative imports remain within extensions/cloudflare: index.ts -> api.ts -> settings.ts/runtime-api.ts, and runtime-api.ts -> settings.ts/s3-backend.ts. There is no additional plugin-owned/shared shipped source outside the root. Package metadata points to index.ts and declares @aws-sdk/client-s3; installed dependency implementations were not audited.",
    "Public plugin-entry exports and DefinePluginEntryOptions.register establish the registration callback as OpenClawPluginApi; the only observed API member is registerStorageProvider. No API/runtime handles escape; no hooks are registered and no runtime members are consumed.",
    "StorageProvider, StorageProviderOpenParams and StorageBackend remain source type dependencies. StorageProviderOpenParams.settings/resolveSecret/signal, backend opts, AWS S3 clients/response objects and AbortSignal methods are not OpenClawPluginApi or PluginRuntime members. Plugin-owned provider/backend implementations are not SDK runtime handles.",
    "The dynamic import of ./runtime-api.js resolves to plugin-owned openR2Backend, not an SDK export or SDK module. It creates no synthetic SDK namespace or dynamic-import dependency.",
    "settings.ts has ordinary value imports for isSecretRef/isValidSecretRef plus inline type SecretInput, so secret-input is mixed; the function exports are runtime and the explicit type export is type-only. Type usages contribute type-reference, calls contribute call.",
    "Manifest storageProviders:r2 is the sole agreed contract identity. id/name/description/categories/activation/configSchema and package installation/build/compatibility fields are metadata rather than contract identities. SDK implementation contracts were consulted only for provenance and are outside plugin file coverage."
  ]
